;; One mutation per invariant. `:find` must occur EXACTLY ONCE in `:file` —
;; `tools/mutate.cljk` refuses otherwise, because a mutation that landed in a
;; comment or a second call site produces a red suite that proves nothing.
;;
;; ## SCOPE
;;
;; Covers what this authoring tier promises: that the enum validator refuses
;; and says which value it refused, that `normalize3` does not hand back NaN
;; for a zero vector, that the three-point presets still carry the numbers
;; the Rust `LightSpec::three_point_*` carries, that `->jsonld` emits the
;; snake_case keys `MangakaScene::from_jsonld` reads, and that `->json`
;; serializes the PROJECTION and not the authored map.
;;
;; It does NOT cover the Rust side of any of this. Every claim of the form
;; "this mirrors Rust variant X" is checked here only against the strings in
;; this file — there is no cross-repository fixture, so a clean run of this
;; table means "the projection is internally measured" and NOT "the projection
;; still matches the crate". It also does not cover `add-prop`, `set-camera`,
;; `add-light` and `set-environment`, which are one-line `assoc`/`update`s.
;;
;; ⚠ THIS HARNESS RUNS `kbb -M:test`, THE JVM HALF ONLY.
;;
;; That matters more here than in most repos, because `->json` is a reader
;; conditional and its `:cljs` branch is the only runtime-specific line in the
;; library. `:the-cljs-json-branch-is-not-measured-by-this-harness` below is
;; in the table precisely to demonstrate that, and it is EXPECTED TO SURVIVE.
;; The `:cljs` half is run by `test/run_portable.cljk` and must be run
;; separately; mutating that branch by hand and running the nbb suite reddens
;; four tests (measured 2026-08-18, recorded under that entry).
;;
;; ## The blind run, and what it found
;;
;; The table was written against the source's invariants before the suite was
;; read. The first run scored 6 killed / 3 survived, and both unexpected
;; survivors were real gaps rather than bad mutations:
;;
;;   :the-key-light-keeps-the-rust-intensity — `three-point-presets` checked
;;     the key light's role and colour and never its intensity.
;;   :jsonld-nests-the-environment-under-snake-case-too — the JSON-LD shape
;;     test named five keys of fourteen, and `ground_size_m` was not one.
;;     Renaming it to camelCase broke nothing here and everything in Rust.
;;
;; Two tests were added, one of them a key-SET assertion rather than another
;; sample of keys, because a test that names fields individually acquires the
;; same gap the next time a field is added. The table now scores 8 killed /
;; 1 survived, and the one survivor is the deliberate entry below.
;;
;; ## Mutations NOT in this table, and why
;;
;; Renaming a `def`/`defn` scores UNMEASURED rather than killed: the rename
;; breaks the callers, the namespace does not load, and a suite that cannot
;; start has not been shown to notice anything. Mutate a VALUE.
[{:id :normalize3-does-not-divide-by-zero
  :invariant "a zero direction normalizes to zero, not to three NaNs"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "    (if (zero? m) [0.0 0.0 0.0] [(/ x m) (/ y m) (/ z m)])))"
  :replace "    (if (zero? 1) [0.0 0.0 0.0] [(/ x m) (/ y m) (/ z m)])))"}

 {:id :check-reports-which-value-it-refused
  :invariant "ex-data names the offending value, not just that one existed"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "{:value v})))"
  :replace "{:value nil})))"}

 {:id :the-key-light-keeps-the-rust-intensity
  :invariant "the three-point presets mirror LightSpec::three_point_*"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find ":colour [1.0 0.96 0.92] :intensity 4.0}))"
  :replace ":colour [1.0 0.96 0.92] :intensity 9.0}))"}

 {:id :an-unknown-emotion-word-falls-back-to-neutral
  :invariant "expression-of is lenient in one specific direction"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "    \"Neutral\"))"
  :replace "    \"Happy\"))"}

 {:id :the-camera-default-fov-is-35
  :invariant "defaults are part of the contract, not decoration"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "fov-deg 35.0 roll-deg 0.0"
  :replace "fov-deg 50.0 roll-deg 0.0"}

 {:id :jsonld-uses-the-snake-case-key-rust-reads
  :invariant "pose_label, not poseLabel — from_jsonld reads serde's spelling"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "\"pose_label\" pose-label"
  :replace "\"poseLabel\" pose-label"}

 {:id :jsonld-nests-the-environment-under-snake-case-too
  :invariant "ground_size_m survives the projection"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "\"ground_size_m\" ground-size-m"
  :replace "\"groundSizeM\" ground-size-m"}

 {:id :json-serializes-the-projection-not-the-authored-map
  :invariant "->json goes through ->jsonld; the authored map has the wrong keys"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "  #?(:clj  (json/write-str (->jsonld s))"
  :replace "  #?(:clj  (json/write-str s)"}

 ;; ⚠ EXPECTED SURVIVOR — kept deliberately, not a gap to be closed here.
 ;;
 ;; `tools/mutate.cljk` drives `kbb -M:test`, so under `:clj` the OTHER
 ;; branch of this reader conditional runs and nothing changes. That is the
 ;; caveat in this file's header turned into evidence instead of a claim.
 ;;
 ;; The same mutation applied by hand and run under nbb, measured 2026-08-18:
 ;;
 ;;   kbb --backend sci --classpath src:test test/run_portable.cljk
 ;;   → Ran 13 tests containing 56 assertions. 4 failures, 0 errors.
 ;;     json-round-trips-the-whole-projection-not-one-key   (2 assertions)
 ;;     json-text-differs-between-runtimes-on-whole-doubles (2 assertions)
 ;;
 ;; The invariant IS covered; it is covered by the other runner. Two tests
 ;; that look like they should have reddened did not, and the reason is worth
 ;; keeping: `clj->js` turns the AUTHORED map's keyword keys into the same
 ;; strings the projection uses for `:biome` and `:camera`, so
 ;; `json-writes-null-for-an-absent-camera-not-an-empty-object` and
 ;; `json-escapes-a-string-that-would-otherwise-break-the-document` still
 ;; pass against the unprojected value. A spot check on one key is not a
 ;; check that the projection ran.
 {:id :the-cljs-json-branch-is-not-measured-by-this-harness
  :invariant "a :cljs branch is invisible to a JVM mutation run"
  :file "src/kami/mangaka/scene.cljk"
  :find "     :cljs (js/JSON.stringify (clj->js (->jsonld s)))))"
  :replace "     :cljs (js/JSON.stringify (clj->js s))))"}]
